// EXPECT: E0246 — an overload for two types this file does not own (ADR-0048 §3)
// The orphan rule: at least one operand must be a struct, union or enum declared *here*. Without
// it an `#import` could silently change what `+` means for `s64`, which is the action-at-a-distance
// ADR-0014 §3 already refused when it made import order stop deciding behaviour. It would also make
// two modules overloading the same builtin pair a conflict with no principled winner.
operator + :: (a: s64, b: s64) -> s64 {
    return a;
}

main :: () {
}
